      "summaries": {
        "en": "Twenty is an open-source CRM platform that provides a community-driven alternative to proprietary systems like Salesforce, addressing the need for customizable and transparent customer relationship management. It's built as a TypeScript monorepo using NestJS and GraphQL, offering modular architecture that enables developers to extend functionality through plugins and integrations. You can deploy it with PostgreSQL for data storage, customize workflows for sales or marketing pipelines, or contribute to its development by tackling labeled issues on GitHub.",
        "zh": "Twenty 是一个开源 CRM 平台，旨在为 Salesforce 等专有系统提供由社区驱动的现代化替代方案，解决企业对可定制、透明客户关系管理工具的需求。该项目采用 TypeScript 单仓库架构，基于 NestJS 和 GraphQL 构建，其模块化设计允许开发者通过插件灵活扩展功能，例如集成营销自动化或自定义销售流程。你可以使用 PostgreSQL 部署它来管理客户数据，根据业务需求调整管道阶段，或参与社区开发，通过处理 GitHub 上标记的议题来改进功能。",
        "es": "Twenty is an open-source CRM platform that provides a community-driven alternative to proprietary systems like Salesforce, addressing the need for customizable and transparent customer relationship management. It's built as a TypeScript monorepo using NestJS and GraphQL, offering modular architecture that enables developers to extend functionality through plugins and integrations. You can deploy it with PostgreSQL for data storage, customize workflows for sales or marketing pipelines, or contribute to its development by tackling labeled issues on GitHub.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "twenty stands out for crm, crm-system, and customer in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Twenty is an open-source CRM platform that provides a community-driven alternative to proprietary systems like Salesforce, addressing the need for customizable and transparent customer relationship management. It's built as a TypeScript monorepo using NestJS and GraphQL, offering modular architecture that enables developers to extend functionality through plugins and integrations. You can deploy it with PostgreSQL for data storage, customize workflows for sales or marketing pipelines, or contribute to its development by tackling labeled issues on GitHub.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
